# L4DEL overlay for the PFR corpus (Polynomial Freiman-Ruzsa). Sidecar notes; the upstream repository is untouched.
# Facts below come from reading the declarations and their docstrings at the pinned checkout. No `sorry` was found in PFR/.

@file PFR/Main.lean

@decl PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Polynomial Freiman-Ruzsa conjecture (characteristic 2)
-- L4DEL: intuition: A finite set in an F2-vector space with small doubling is covered by about K^12 translates of a subgroup no bigger than the set itself.
-- L4DEL: step: Statement: if A is a nonempty finite subset of an F2-vector space G and |A + A| is at most K times |A|, there are a subspace H and a finite set c with fewer than 2 * K^12 elements such that A lies inside c + H and |H| is at most |A|.
-- L4DEL: step: If G is infinite, the proof first replaces G by the span of A, which is finite, runs the finite case there, and pushes the answer back along the inclusion.
-- L4DEL: step: In the finite case it applies the covering lemma PFR_conjecture_aux, which gives H and a covering set c with |c| at most K^(13/2) |A|^(1/2) |H|^(-1/2) and |H| comparable to |A| up to a factor K^11.
-- L4DEL: step: If |H| is at most |A| that H already works. Otherwise it picks a subspace H' of H with |A|/2 < |H'| at most |A| and covers H by cosets of H' using a transversal, which multiplies the number of translates by |H|/|H'| and gives the bound below 2 * K^12.
-- L4DEL: prereq: PFR_conjecture_aux, PFR_conjecture_pos_aux'
-- L4DEL: see: PFR_conjecture_improv, entropic_PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: term: doubling constant = the number K bounding |A + A| / |A| from above; small K means A is close to a subgroup.
-- L4DEL: term: elementary abelian 2-group = an abelian group in which every element has order at most 2; the same thing as a vector space over the field with two elements, here a module over ZMod 2.

@decl PFR_conjecture_aux
-- L4DEL: title: Covering lemma behind PFR
-- L4DEL: intuition: A set of doubling K is covered by few cosets of a subgroup whose size is within a power of K of the set's size.
-- L4DEL: step: Pick a uniform random variable UA on A and show its Ruzsa distance to itself is at most log K, using rdist_le_of_isUniform_of_card_sub_le.
-- L4DEL: step: Apply the entropic PFR theorem with parameter 1/9 to get a subgroup H whose uniform distribution is within 11/2 log K of UA in Ruzsa distance.
-- L4DEL: step: Compare entropies of independent copies of UA and UH to get that |A| and |H| agree up to a factor K^11.
-- L4DEL: step: Find a point x0 where VA - VH has large probability, which says A meets the coset H + x0 in at least K^(-11/2) |A|^(1/2) |H|^(1/2) points.
-- L4DEL: step: Cover A by translates of A' - A' (A' = A meet (H + x0)), which sits inside H, using the Ruzsa covering lemma. The number of translates is at most K^(13/2) |A|^(1/2) |H|^(-1/2).
-- L4DEL: prereq: entropic_PFR_conjecture, rdist_le_of_isUniform_of_card_sub_le
-- L4DEL: see: PFR_conjecture

@decl rdist_le_of_isUniform_of_card_sub_le
-- L4DEL: title: Small doubling gives small self Ruzsa distance
-- L4DEL: intuition: A uniform random variable on a set with |A - A| at most K|A| is within log K of itself in Ruzsa distance.
-- L4DEL: step: Take two independent copies U and U' of the uniform variable on A.
-- L4DEL: step: The entropy of U - U' is at most log |A - A|, because U - U' takes values in A - A.
-- L4DEL: step: The entropy of a uniform variable on A is log |A|, so d[U ; U'] = H[U - U'] - H[U]/2 - H[U']/2 is at most log |A - A| - log |A|, which is at most log K.
-- L4DEL: prereq: rdist
-- L4DEL: see: rdist_triangle
-- L4DEL: term: Ruzsa distance = for random variables X and Y in an abelian group, d[X ; Y] = H[X' - Y'] - H[X']/2 - H[Y']/2, where X' and Y' are independent copies and H is Shannon entropy in nats.

@file PFR/EntropyPFR.lean

@decl entropic_PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Entropic PFR (constants 11 and 6)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Any two random variables in an F2-vector space are within a constant multiple of their Ruzsa distance of a uniform distribution on some subgroup.
-- L4DEL: step: Statement: for finite G of characteristic 2 and a package of two G-valued variables X01, X02 with parameter eta = 1/9, there is a subspace H and a uniform variable U on H with d[X01 ; U] + d[X02 ; U] at most 11 d[X01 ; X02], and each of d[X01 ; U] and d[X02 ; U] at most 6 d[X01 ; X02].
-- L4DEL: step: Take a pair X1, X2 minimizing the tau functional (tau_minimizer_exists). The theorem tau_strictly_decreases then forces d[X1 ; X2] = 0 when eta = 1/9.
-- L4DEL: step: Zero Ruzsa distance means X1 and X2 are uniform on cosets of a common subgroup (exists_isUniform_of_rdist_eq_zero), which gives H and U.
-- L4DEL: step: The distances from the original variables to U follow from minimality of tau and the Ruzsa triangle inequality (rdist_triangle), finished by linear arithmetic.
-- L4DEL: prereq: tau_minimizer_exists, tau_strictly_decreases, rdist_triangle, exists_isUniform_of_rdist_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: see: entropic_PFR_conjecture_improv
-- L4DEL: term: tau functional = tau[X1 ; X2] = d[X1 ; X2] + eta d[X01 ; X1] + eta d[X02 ; X2], where X01 and X02 are the fixed reference variables of the package; minimizing it is the engine of the entropic proof.

@file PFR/ImprovedPFR.lean

@decl entropic_PFR_conjecture_improv
-- L4DEL: title: Entropic PFR, improved constants (10 and 11/2)
-- L4DEL: intuition: The same entropic statement with eta = 1/8, giving sum of distances at most 10 d and each distance at most 11/2 d.
-- L4DEL: step: Take a tau-minimizing pair whose Ruzsa distance is already zero (tau_minimizer_exists_rdist_eq_zero). Its proof uses the sharper estimate tau_strictly_decreases' valid for 8 * eta < 1, plus a limiting argument for eta = 1/8.
-- L4DEL: step: As before, get a subgroup H and uniform U from zero Ruzsa distance.
-- L4DEL: step: Minimality of tau against the swapped pair and two uses of the triangle inequality give the 10 bound on the sum and the 11/2 bound on each distance.
-- L4DEL: prereq: tau_minimizer_exists_rdist_eq_zero, rdist_triangle, exists_isUniform_of_rdist_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: see: entropic_PFR_conjecture

@decl PFR_conjecture_improv
-- L4DEL: title: PFR with exponent 11
-- L4DEL: intuition: The improved form of PFR: fewer than 2 * K^11 cosets of a subgroup of size at most |A| cover A.
-- L4DEL: step: Statement: if A is nonempty and finite in an F2-vector space with |A + A| at most K |A|, there are a subspace H and a finite c with fewer than 2 * K^11 elements, |H| at most |A|, and A inside c + H.
-- L4DEL: step: Reduce to finite G by passing to the span of A, as in PFR_conjecture.
-- L4DEL: step: Use PFR_conjecture_improv_aux (covering by K^6 |A|^(1/2) |H|^(-1/2) cosets, |H| within K^10 of |A|), which is derived from entropic_PFR_conjecture_improv.
-- L4DEL: step: Shrink H to a subspace of size between |A|/2 and |A| when |H| exceeds |A|, and cover H by its cosets.
-- L4DEL: prereq: PFR_conjecture_improv_aux, entropic_PFR_conjecture_improv
-- L4DEL: see: PFR_conjecture

@file PFR/WeakPFR.lean

@decl weak_PFR_int
-- L4DEL: title: Weak PFR over the integers
-- L4DEL: intuition: A finite set A in a lattice with |A - A| at most K|A| has a subset of density K^(-17) that lies in an affine subspace of dimension O(log K).
-- L4DEL: step: Statement: G is a finitely generated free Z-module, A is a finite nonempty subset with |A - A| at most K |A|. There is A' inside A with |A'| at least K^(-17) |A| and affine dimension at most (40 / log 2) log K.
-- L4DEL: step: Show K is positive and that the self distance of the uniform distribution on A is at most log K, using ProbabilityTheory.setRuzsaDist_le and the entropy bound log |A - A| at most log K + log |A|.
-- L4DEL: step: Apply weak_PFR, which in turn rests on weak_PFR_asymm.
-- L4DEL: prereq: weak_PFR, weak_PFR_asymm, ProbabilityTheory.setRuzsaDist_le
-- L4DEL: see: weak_PFR_int_sumset, PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: term: affine dimension = the dimension of the smallest affine subspace over the integers containing a set, written AffineSpace.finrank over the integers in the source.

@decl weak_PFR_int_sumset
-- L4DEL: title: Weak PFR from a sumset hypothesis
-- L4DEL: intuition: The same weak PFR conclusion when the hypothesis is |A + A| at most K|A|, at the cost of squaring K: density K^(-34) and dimension at most (80 / log 2) log K.
-- L4DEL: step: Ruzsa's triangle inequality for sets gives |A - A| |A| at most |A + A|^2, so |A - A| is at most K^2 |A|.
-- L4DEL: step: Apply weak_PFR_int with K^2 in place of K.
-- L4DEL: step: Rewrite the exponents: (K^2)^(-17) = K^(-34) and the logarithm of K^2 is twice log K.
-- L4DEL: prereq: weak_PFR_int
-- L4DEL: see: weak_PFR_int

@file PFR/HomPFR.lean

@decl homomorphism_pfr
-- L4DEL: title: Homomorphism PFR
-- L4DEL: intuition: A map between F2-vector spaces that is almost additive differs from a true homomorphism by a set of size at most |S|^10.
-- L4DEL: step: Statement: if f(x+y) - f(x) - f(y) always lies in a set S, there are a group homomorphism phi and a set T with |T| at most |S|^10 such that f(x) - phi(x) lies in T for all x.
-- L4DEL: step: Consider the graph A of f inside G x G'. Then A + A sits inside A - ({0} x S), so |A + A| is at most |S| |A|.
-- L4DEL: step: Apply a PFR covering lemma (better_PFR_conjecture_aux) to get a subgroup H of G x G' and a covering set c of A.
-- L4DEL: step: Use Goursat's lemma (goursat) to describe H as a graph-like subgroup over phi, then take T as the image of c + ({0} x H1) under the map (x, y) to y - phi(x).
-- L4DEL: prereq: goursat
-- L4DEL: see: PFR_conjecture

