@decl approx_hom_pfr
-- L4DEL: title: Let $G, G'$ be finite abelian $2$-groups
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $G, G'$ be finite abelian $2$-groups. Let $f : G \to G'$ be a function, and suppose that there is a proportion of at least $K^{-1}$ pairs $(x,y) \in G^2$ such that $$ f(x+y) = f(x) + f(y).$$ Then there exists a homomorphism $\phi : G \to G'$ and a constant $c \in G'$ such that $f(x) = \phi(x)+c$ for at least $|G| / (2 ^ {144} * K ^ {122})$ values of $x \in G$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

