@decl condRuzsaDist_diff_le
-- L4DEL: title: Let `X, Y, Z` be random variables taking values in some abelian group, and with `Y, Z` independent
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let `X, Y, Z` be random variables taking values in some abelian group, and with `Y, Z` independent. Then we have `d[X ; Y + Z] - d[X ; Y] ≤ 1/2 (H[Y+ Z] - H[Y])` $$= \tfrac{1}{2} d[Y ; Z] + \tfrac{1}{4} H[Z] - \tfrac{1}{4} H[Y]$$ and $$d[X ; Y|Y+ Z] - d[X ; Y] \leq \tfrac{1}{2} \bigl(H[Y+ Z] - H[Z]\bigr)$$ $$= \tfrac{1}{2} d[Y ; Z] + \tfrac{1}{4} H[Y] - \tfrac{1}{4} H[Z]$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

