@file PFR/ImprovedPFR.lean
@decl PFR_conjecture_improv_aux
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: PFR_conjecture_improv_aux
-- L4DEL: intuition: Auxiliary statement towards the polynomial Freiman-Ruzsa (PFR) conjecture: if $A$ is a subset of an elementary abelian 2-group of doubling constant at most $K$, then there exists a subgroup $H$ such that $A$ can be covered by at most $K^6 |A|^{1/2} / |H|^{1/2}$ cosets of $H$, and $H$ has the same cardinality as $A$ up to a multiplicative factor $K^10$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/ImprovedPFR.lean
@decl tau_minimizer_exists_rdist_eq_zero
-- L4DEL: title: For `p.η ≤ 1/8`, there exist τ-minimizers `X₁, X₂` at zero Rusza distance
-- L4DEL: intuition: For `p.η ≤ 1/8`, there exist τ-minimizers `X₁, X₂` at zero Rusza distance. For `p.η < 1/8`, all minimizers are fine, by `tau_strictly_decreases'`. For `p.η = 1/8`, we use a limit of minimizers for `η < 1/8`, which exists by compactness.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/ImprovedPFR.lean
