@file PFR/MoreRuzsaDist.lean
@decl cond_multiDist_chainRule
-- L4DEL: title: Let `π : G → H` be a homomorphism of abelian groups
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let `π : G → H` be a homomorphism of abelian groups. Let `I` be a finite index set and let `X_[m]` be a tuple of `G`-valued random variables. Let `Y_[m]` be another tuple of random variables (not necessarily `G`-valued). Suppose that the pairs `(X_i, Y_i)` are jointly independent of one another (but `X_i` need not be independent of `Y_i`). Then `D[X_[m] | Y_[m]] = D[X_[m] ,|, π(X_[m]), Y_[m]] + D[π(X_[m]) ,| , Y_[m]]` `+ I[∑ i, X_i : π(X_[m]) ; | ; π(∑ i, X_i), Y_[m]]`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/MoreRuzsaDist.lean
@decl condMultiDist_eq
-- L4DEL: title: If `(X_i, Y_i)`, `1 ≤ i ≤ m` are independent, then `D[X_[m] | Y_[m]] = H[∑ i, X_i | (Y_1, ..., Y_m)] - 1/m * ∑ i, H[X_i | Y_i]`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `(X_i, Y_i)`, `1 ≤ i ≤ m` are independent, then `D[X_[m] | Y_[m]] = H[∑ i, X_i | (Y_1, ..., Y_m)] - 1/m * ∑ i, H[X_i | Y_i]`
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/MoreRuzsaDist.lean
@decl condMultiDist_eq'
-- L4DEL: title: If `(X_i, Y_i)`, `1 ≤ i ≤ m` are independent, then `D[X_[m] | Y_[m]] = ∑_{(y_i)_{1 ≤ i ≤ m}} P(Y_i=y_i ∀ i) D[(X_i | Y_i=y_i ∀ i)_{i=1}^m]`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `(X_i, Y_i)`, `1 ≤ i ≤ m` are independent, then `D[X_[m] | Y_[m]] = ∑_{(y_i)_{1 ≤ i ≤ m}} P(Y_i=y_i ∀ i) D[(X_i | Y_i=y_i ∀ i)_{i=1}^m]`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

