@decl cor_multiDist_chainRule
-- L4DEL: title: Let `G` be an abelian group and let `m ≥ 2`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let `G` be an abelian group and let `m ≥ 2`. Suppose that `X_{i,j}`, `1 ≤ i, j ≤ m`, are independent `G`-valued random variables. Then `I[(∑ i, X_{i,j})_{j=1}^m : (∑ j, X_{i,j})_{i=1}^m | ∑ i j, X_{i,j}]` is less than `∑_{j=1}^{m - 1} (D[(X_{i, j})_{i=1}^m]` `- D[(X_{i, j})_{i = 1}^m | (X_{i,j} + ... + X_{i,m})_{i=1}^m])` `+ D[(X_{i,m})_{i=1}^m] - D[(∑ j, X_{i,j})_{i=1}^m],` where all the multidistances here involve the indexing set `{1, ..., m}`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

