@decl better_PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: better_PFR_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $A \subset {\bf F}_2^n$ is finite non-empty with $|A+A| \leq K|A|$, then there exists a subgroup $H$ of ${\bf F}_2^n$ with $|H| \leq |A|$ such that $A$ can be covered by at most $2K^9$ translates of $H$. The ambient group need not be finite, in which case `H` and `c` are finite.
