@decl torsion_PFR
-- L4DEL: title: Suppose that $G$ is an abelian group of torsion $m$ (not necessarily finite)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Suppose that $G$ is an abelian group of torsion $m$ (not necessarily finite). If $A \subset G$ is a finite non-empty set with $|A+A| \leq K|A|$, then $A$ can be covered by at most $m K^{256 m^3+1}$ translates of a finite subspace $H$ of $G$ with $|H| \leq |A|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/TorsionEndgame.lean
@decl torsion_PFR_conjecture_aux
-- L4DEL: title: Suppose that $G$ is a finite abelian group of torsion $m$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Suppose that $G$ is a finite abelian group of torsion $m$. If $A \subset G$ is non-empty and $|A+A| \leq K|A|$, then $A$ can be covered by at most $K^{128 m^3+1} |A|^{1/2}/|H|^{1/2}$ translates of a subspace $H$ of $G$ with $|H|/|A| \in [K^{-256 m^3}, K^{256 m^3}]$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file PFR/WeakPFR.lean
@decl app_ent_PFR'
-- L4DEL: title: Let $G=\mathbb{F}_2^n$ and `X, Y` be `G`-valued random variables such that \[\mathbb{H}(X)+\mathbb{H}(Y)> (20/\alpha) d[X;Y],\] for some $\alpha > 0$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $G=\mathbb{F}_2^n$ and `X, Y` be `G`-valued random variables such that \[\mathbb{H}(X)+\mathbb{H}(Y)> (20/\alpha) d[X;Y],\] for some $\alpha > 0$. There is a non-trivial subgroup $H\leq G$ such that \[\log \lvert H\rvert <(1+\alpha)/2 (\mathbb{H}(X)+\mathbb{H}(Y))\] and \[\mathbb{H}(\psi(X))+\mathbb{H}(\psi(Y))< \alpha (\mathbb{H}(X)+\mathbb{H}(Y))\] where $\psi:G\to G/H$ is the natural projection homomorphism.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

