-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: weak_PFR
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $A\subseteq \mathbb{Z}^d$ is a finite non-empty set with $d[U_A;U_A]\leq \log K$ then there exists a non-empty $A'\subseteq A$ such that $\lvert A'\rvert\geq K^{-17}\lvert A\rvert$ and $\dim A'\leq \frac{40}{\log 2} \log K$.
